---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout title="About Todd Kashdan" current="about">
  <div class="wrap page-hero" style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:1.2fr .9fr; gap:44px; align-items:center;">
    <div>
      <p class="kicker">Psychologist &middot; Scientist &middot; Author &middot; Speaker</p>
      <h1>My life is devoted to the science of human <em>fulfillment</em>.</h1>
      <p class="lead">Awarded the 2013 Distinguished Early Career Researcher Award by the American Psychological Association, Todd Kashdan is among the world's top experts on the psychology of curiosity, purpose in life, strengths, psychological flexibility, and social relationships. His research has been featured in Harvard Business Review, The New York Times, Fast Company, Forbes, and NPR's Hidden Brain.</p>
      <div style="display:flex; gap:14px; flex-wrap:wrap;">
        <a class="btn solid" href="/speaking/">Invite Todd to Speak</a>
        <a class="btn ghost" href="mailto:todd@toddkashdan.com">Email Todd</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div><img src="/images/img_019.jpeg" alt="Todd Kashdan signing a copy of The Art of Insubordination for a fan after a talk" style="border-radius:10px; box-shadow:0 30px 70px rgba(0,0,0,.55);" /></div>
  </div>

  <div class="strip wrap">
    <div><div class="n">250+</div><div class="l">Peer-reviewed scientific papers on well-being and human performance</div></div>
    <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=rC3rn04AAAAJ&hl=en&oi=ao" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><div class="n">61,000+</div><div class="l">Citations on Google Scholar &rarr;</div></a>
    <div><div class="n">2013</div><div class="l">APA Distinguished Early Career Researcher Award</div></div>
    <div><div class="n">2010</div><div class="l">GMU Distinguished Faculty Member of the Year, for teaching and mentoring</div></div>
  </div>

  <div class="section wrap">
    <div class="sec-h"><h2>The short version</h2></div>
    <p class="lead" style="max-width:70ch;">As a Professor of Psychology at George Mason University, Todd translates state-of-the-art science into practical applications people can use in everyday life, known for an energetic and disarming communication style. He gave a <a href="#" style="color:var(--gold); font-weight:700;">TEDx talk</a> on psychological flexibility. Over 5 million readers have read his blog post in Psychology Today and his best-selling Substack newsletter, <em style="color:var(--gold); font-style:normal;">Provoked</em>.</p>
    <p class="lead" style="max-width:70ch;">After earning a Ph.D. in clinical psychology in 2004, Todd founded the Well-Being Lab at George Mason University, which has since produced over 250 peer-reviewed journal articles on well-being, resilience, meaning and purpose in life, curiosity, and managing anxiety. He ranks among the top 1% of scholars worldwide.</p>
    <p class="lead" style="max-width:70ch;">Todd has authored five books, including <em style="color:var(--gold); font-style:normal;">Curious?</em>, <em style="color:var(--gold); font-style:normal;">The Upside of Your Dark Side</em>, and <em style="color:var(--gold); font-style:normal;">The Art of Insubordination</em>. His next book, <em style="color:var(--gold); font-style:normal;">On Purpose: The Science of Building a Meaningful Life</em>, arrives from Ten Street Press in 2027.</p>
    <p class="lead" style="max-width:70ch; color:var(--dim); font-style:italic;">Off the clock: Todd exercises relentlessly for the freedom to consume copious amounts of steak, whiskey, and Italian Rainbow Square cookies. He is a twin and the father of twins (plus one more), with plans to populate the world with great conversationalists.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="section wrap">
    <div class="news">
      <div>
        <p class="news-eyebrow">Connect</p>
        <h2>Speaking requests or questions?</h2>
        <p>Email Todd directly, or reach out about a speaking engagement through The Lavin Agency.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="news-cta">
        <a class="btn solid" href="mailto:todd@toddkashdan.com">Email Todd</a>
        <a class="btn ghost" href="/speaking/">Speaking &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
